"notes":[
"Controller support: Xbox, PlayStation and Switch pads and the Steam Deck's own controls (Steam Input \"Gamepad\"). Pick one up and the game shows its buttons; touch the keyboard or mouse and the keys come back.",
"Everywhere: a stick moves the cursor, A clicks (hold A to drag), B goes back. In menus the d-pad jumps between buttons and the triggers / bumpers scroll. Text boxes get a small on-screen keyboard (on a Deck with Steam running, Steam's own keyboard opens instead).",
"In a match: Left stick ......... walk (let go: stop)          Right stick .... cursor (push an edge: pan the camera) LB / RB / LT / RT .. abilities Q / W / E / R: hold to aim (the right stick moves the aim), let go to cast A .................. click (select, Armory, every button) X .................. attack the nearest monster; with the left stick held: attack-move that way B .................. back: cancel the aim, close the open panel; otherwise Stop Y (tap) ............ the sends & buildings wheel: point a stick, A builds / opens / sends (again and again), X switches the rift, B steps back and closes Y (hold) + ......... shoulder or trigger: learn that ability \u00b7 d-pad: ally commands (up help, right boss, down crystal, left lanes) \u00b7 A: vote \"start next round\" \u00b7 X: hold \u00b7 B: stop \u00b7 R3: jump to an enemy hero \u00b7 View: crystal upgrades \u00b7 L3: auto-attack \u00b7 Menu: watch duel D-pad .............. up: potion (dead: buy back) \u00b7 down: Armory \u00b7 left / right: first / second active item R3 ................. camera to your hero \u00b7 Menu: pause \u00b7 View: scoreboard (tap toggles, hold peeks)",
"Settings > Controller: on/off, southpaw (sticks swapped), button glyphs (auto, Xbox, PlayStation, Steam Deck, Nintendo), stick dead zone, cursor and camera speed, vibration, and every button above can be rebound.",
"Light rumble on heavy hits, kills, your death and a boss's arrival (Settings > Controller > Vibration).",
"The tutorial speaks controller when you play it on one."
]
}